From 0a593b53f0be42dc850caa209ec3c05c34f1c888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:45:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] 027 (TKGeomBase): GenExtPS keeps the stock grid walk and
 defers the edge evaluations, sorted by V

The V-major walk of the previous commit removed the B-spline cache rebuilds but walked the grid
arrays across rows; measured on the whole-screw oblique section it was no faster (profile: RebuildCache
gone, BuildGrid self time up). Now the grid is walked in the stock U-major order (streaming memory),
and for an edge whose closest point is inside, computeEdgeDeferred027 (ComputeEdgeParameters without
the evaluation, same arithmetic expression by expression) stores the parameters; the surface points
are then evaluated in (V column, U row) order, so consecutive evaluations share a V span.

Measured (native harness, sequential, one run): face 149 5.79 -> 4.28 s, face 150 5.46 -> 4.57 s,
whole-screw oblique section 68.4 -> 64.6 s (with the two TKBO commits in both).

EXTREMA_027_VERIFY: every edge recomputed with the stock ComputeEdgeParameters and compared bit for
bit; EXTREMA_027_MUTANT: the last deferred point is not evaluated (negative control).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
